 How WebSocket Works
Step 1: Client sends HTTP Upgrade Request

Initially, communication starts as HTTP.

GET /chat HTTP/1.1
Host: example.com
Upgrade: websocket
Connection: Upgrade

Client requests:

"Please upgrade this HTTP connection to WebSocket."

Step 2: Server accepts

Server responds:

HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols
Upgrade: websocket
Connection: Upgrade

Connection gets upgraded.

Step 3: Persistent Connection Created

Now both client and server remain connected continuously.

Client <===================> Server

No repeated requests are required.

Full Duplex Communication

WebSocket supports Full Duplex Communication.

Meaning:

Client can send data anytime.
Server can send data anytime.

Both can communicate simultaneously.

Client <--------> Server

Unlike HTTP:

Client ------> Server
Client <------ Server